@{
  PdpSiteRazorModel psrm = Model.PSRM;
  NpdsClientWrace npdscw = Model.NPDSCW;
}

<h4>REST API Service Help</h4>

@if (PDPSS.AppUseDebugRouting)
{
  <p>
    Help on the NPDS web service API available at this site
    can also be obtained by appending the querystring key "help" to any URL derived from the site base
    address. Additional URL routing information can be obtained by appending the querystring key "debug"
    to the URL. These keys can be used independently or in combination as shown in the following examples:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><a href="@npdscw.UrlHelp">@npdscw.UrlHelp</a></li>
    <li><a href="@npdscw.UrlDebug">@npdscw.UrlDebug</a></li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Help information displayed by use of the "help" querystring key provides the syntax for all URLs together
    with live examples that demonstrate each URL. Debug diagnostics displayed by use of the "debug" querystring
    key provide the defaults and constraints for all routes together with a live matching test of the requested
    URL against all routes that shows whether each route is "found", "matched", or "unmatched". Note that
    the "found" route is the first "matched" route.
  </p>
}

<p>
  Querystring key-value pairs valid for all NPDS web service URLs include:
</p>
<ul>
  <li>
    Logical switches
    <ul>
      <li>
        "af": Archive Format with af={1|0} or af={true|false} turns on/off response that includes additional content for archiving
      </li>
      <li>"cf": Check Format with cf={1|0} or tf={true|false} turns on/off response with schema validation</li>
      <li>
        "ef": Echo Format with ef={1|0} or ef={true|false} turns on/off response that includes a copy of the request URL
      </li>
      <li>
        "qf": Query Format with qf={1|0} or qf={true|false} turns on/off case-sensitive find intended for unique exact match 
        instead of case-insensitive search for multiple partial matches
      </li>
      <li>"vf": Verbose Format with ef={1|0} or ef={true|false} turns on/off response with more detailed information</li>
    </ul>
  </li>
  <li>
    Integer values
    <ul>
      <li>"lc": List Count with lc={value} sets maximum number of records returned in the response</li>
    </ul>
  </li>
  <li>
    String switches
    <ul>
      <li>"mf": Message Format with mf={none|json|xml|xhtml} sets the response format for records returned in the response if supported by the server accessed.</li>
      <li>
        "rf": Resrep Format with rf={core|nexus|portal|doors|scribe} sets the resource representation format for the
        records returned in the response if supported by the server accessed; see pages 180-181 of the
        <a href="~/pub/docs/FutInt2010v2n2p156-189Taswell.pdf" target="_blank">Metadata about Metadata article</a>
        in Future Internet.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </li>
</ul>
<p>
  Querystring keys valid for NPDS query URLs include:
</p>
<ul>
  <li>"enam": enam={value} filters records on the EntityName field</li>
  <li>"enat": enat={value} filters records on the EntityNature field</li>
  <li>"etag": etag={value} filters records on the EntityPrincipalTag field</li>
  <li>"etyp": etyp={value} filters records on the EntityType field</li>
  <li>
    "tagany": tagany={value} filters records on the EntityTag fields (either the EntityPrincipalTag or EntityAliasTags)
  </li>
  <li>
    "tagsup": tagsup={value} filters records on the EntitySupportingTag fields
  </li>
  <li>
    "labany": labany={value} filters records on the EntityLabel fields (either the EntityCanonicalLabel or
    EntityAliasLabels)
  </li>
  <li>
    "labsup": labsup={value} filters records on the EntitySupportingLabel fields
  </li>
  <li>
    "labcan": labcan={value} filters records on the EntityCanonicalLabel field
  </li>
  <li>
    "labals": labals={value} filters records on the EntityAliasLabel fields
  </li>
</ul>

<p>
  Forwarding/caching only partially implemented at <a href="https://www.portaldoors.org/" target="_blank">www.portaldoors.org</a>
  currently not all requests should return records from all sites;
  please check also the originating authoritative site.
</p>
